  "notes": [
   "Step 1 parts were correct and are unchanged: Uno, breadboard, MIDI jack, two 220 ohm resistors, three jumper wires.",
   "Circuit follows the tutorial: MIDI pin 5 goes through a 220 ohm resistor (r1) to digital pin 1 (TX). MIDI pin 2 goes to GND. MIDI pin 4 goes through a 220 ohm resistor (r2) to +5V.",
   "The jack's five legs sit in neighbouring holes of row a in the top half, columns 6-10, in pin order 1-5. Pins 1 and 3 are unused but are physically in the board.",
   "Each resistor spans the centre gap in its own column (r1 in column 10, r2 in column 9). The TX and 5V wires land in the bottom-half strip of the same column.",
   "The ground wire goes to column 7, the strip holding jack pin 2.",
   "The image shows the GND wire at the digital-header GND next to AREF. I mapped it to uno GND.3, assuming that is the digital-header GND.",
   "The short coloured legs in the image between the jack and resistors are treated as jack legs, not separate wires."
  ]
 },
